Chapter: Sixlowpan

 6LoWPAN (RFC 4944 / 6282), the adaptation layer that carries IPv6 over
 IEEE 802.15.4 so constrained mesh nodes (Thread, Zigbee IP) can speak
 IP. Each adaptation header starts with a dispatch byte. This chapter
 builds the IPHC (IP header compression) base header -- the two-byte
 field of compression flags -- and the fragmentation headers (FRAG1 and
 subsequent FRAGN) that split a datagram larger than one 802.15.4 frame.

Section: Dispatch Bytes

  lowpan-dispatch-nalp : Integer = #00
  lowpan-dispatch-ipv6 : Integer = #41
  lowpan-dispatch-frag1 : Integer = #C0
  lowpan-dispatch-fragn : Integer = #E0
  lowpan-dispatch-mesh : Integer = #80

Section: IPHC Base Header

 The IPHC base is two bytes. The first: 011 (dispatch), traffic class
 and flow label compression (TF, 2 bits), next-header compression (NH,
 1 bit), hop-limit compression (HLIM, 2 bits). The second: context
 identifier extension (CID), source address compression (SAC), source
 address mode (SAM, 2 bits), multicast (M), destination address
 compression (DAC), destination address mode (DAM, 2 bits).

  lowpan-iphc : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  lowpan-iphc (tf) (nh) (hlim) (cid) (sac) (sam) (m) (dac) (dam) =
   let byte0 = bit-or #60 (bit-or (bit-shl tf 3) (bit-or (bit-shl nh 2) hlim))
   in let byte1 = bit-or (bit-shl cid 7) (bit-or (bit-shl sac 6) (bit-or (bit-shl sam 4) (bit-or (bit-shl m 3) (bit-or (bit-shl dac 2) dam))))
   in [byte0, byte1]

Section: Fragmentation

 The FRAG1 header of the first fragment carries the total datagram size
 (11 bits) and a tag identifying the datagram (16 bits). Each FRAGN
 header adds an 8-bit offset in units of eight octets.

  lowpan-frag1 : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  lowpan-frag1 (datagram-size) (tag) =
   [bit-or lowpan-dispatch-frag1 (bit-and (bit-shru datagram-size 8) 7), bit-and datagram-size 255, bit-and (bit-shru tag 8) 255, bit-and tag 255]

  lowpan-fragn : Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  lowpan-fragn (datagram-size) (tag) (offset) =
   [bit-or lowpan-dispatch-fragn (bit-and (bit-shru datagram-size 8) 7), bit-and datagram-size 255, bit-and (bit-shru tag 8) 255, bit-and tag 255, bit-and offset 255]
